<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Salome (daughter of Herodias)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Salome was a Herodian princess, daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodias">Herodias</a> and Herod Philip, named by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/josephus">Josephus</a>. She is identified with the unnamed daughter of Herodias who, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gospels">Gospels</a>, danced before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herod-antipas">Herod Antipas</a> and asked for the head of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-the-baptist">John the Baptist</a>. She married first the tetrarch Philip and then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aristobulus-of-chalcis">Aristobulus of Chalcis</a>, with whom she ruled Lesser <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a>.</p></div>
